// A relaxed store after a release, to the same location in the same thread,
// continues the release sequence in RC11 (Lahav et al., PLDI 2017, §3.2:
// rs ≜ [W]; sb|loc?; [W^⊒rlx]; (rf; rmw)*). The acquire reading it
// synchronises with the release, x := 1 happens-before r2, and the stale read
// of x is forbidden. sMRD synchronises only rf ∩ (W_rel × R_acq), with no
// release sequence beyond the releasing write, so its coherence allows the
// outcome. The witnessing execution elides no write and forwards nothing; the
// difference is the release sequence alone. Same shape as
// rmm-zoo/models/cpp-release-sequences/mp-rs.lit, with relaxed data.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rlx);
  y.store(1, rel);
  y.store(2, rlx)
} ||| {
  r1 := y.load(acq);
  r2 := x.load(rlx)
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 2 && r2 = 0) [RC11]
allow (r1 = 2 && r2 = 0) [sMRD]
